## Purpose
Describe the service here. The generated example stores tenant-scoped items; it exists to prove
authentication, tenancy and health end to end, not to be a product feature.

## What the generator already did
- Added `services/@name@` to the workspace `members`, so `cargo test --workspace` and CI cover it.
- Added `CALL platform.provision_service('@name@');` to
  [`deploy/postgres/bootstrap/004_provision_services.sql`](../../deploy/postgres/bootstrap/004_provision_services.sql),
  so the role, schema and grants exist where the bootstrap runs.
- Gave every route except `/health` the gateway's internal-token check (ADR-0012). Tenant and user
  come from the verified token, never from the request.
- Put every query inside a tenant transaction under row-level security (ADR-0011).
- Wired `timelex_telemetry::init` and `timelex_telemetry::instrument` so requests keep the caller's
  trace and logs are redacted (ADR-0016).

## Contract
- **REST:** `GET /health`, `GET /v1/items`, `POST /v1/items`
- Add the service's real contract under [`contracts/openapi`](../../contracts/openapi) before the
  operations grow, then route it from the gateway.

## Run the tests
Need a throwaway Postgres: see [deploy/postgres/README.md](../../deploy/postgres/README.md).
```
TIMELEX_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres cargo test -p @crate@
```

## Run the service
```
TIMELEX_@UPPER@_DATABASE_URL=postgres://svc_@name@:<password>@127.0.0.1:55433/postgres \
TIMELEX_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_KEYS=k1=<base64 public key> \
TIMELEX_@UPPER@_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8083 \
cargo run -p @crate@
```
The connection string above is a shape, not a working URL: put the real role password in the
environment, never in a file in the repository. Apply migrations first with
`cargo run -p @crate@ -- migrate` and `TIMELEX_MIGRATOR_DATABASE_URL`.

| Variable | Used by | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `TIMELEX_@UPPER@_DATABASE_URL` | serve | connection URL for the `svc_@name@` role |
| `TIMELEX_MIGRATOR_DATABASE_URL` | migrate | connection URL for `timelex_migrator` |
| `TIMELEX_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_KEYS` | serve | gateway public keys (`kid=base64,...`) |
| `TIMELEX_@UPPER@_ADDR` | serve | listen address, default `127.0.0.1:8083` |

